  "notes": "Drawn from N339UP (767-300F, July 2026). Freighters have no windows. The brown starts as a thin wedge on the crown over the wing. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on N339UP: 'Worldwide Services' runs x 0.153 to 0.345, lowercase 0.77 of the capitals; the gold edge and the brown are curves (smooth), and the brown's outline, which crossed itself, now follows the gold's aft edge only.",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximate standard (a few colors from memory). The 2003 livery came with the shield redesign, replacing the 1961 bow-tie shield scheme.",
  "types": {
    "A306": {
      "note": "On the A300-600F the sweep is longer and further forward than the 767's fitted by landmarks: it leaves the crown over the wing's root (the gold line at x 0.29, the brown at 0.345, against 0.41 and 0.48 fitted) and reaches the belly at 0.76-0.785 (N124UP, 2017, fitted to the shape; N158UP, 2024, alike). Its title isn't measured here: the 2017 photo has the old second line under it.",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "sourceRefs": [
